## Common Mistakes to Address

| Mistake | Why It Happens | Correction |
|---------|----------------|------------|
| Excessive DOMS causing dropout | Too much volume too soon | Start with low volume (2×5 reps), progress gradually over weeks  |
| Poor long-term adherence | Programme feels tedious or is not integrated | Integrate into warm-up routine; make it a team habit  |
| Only performing NHE | Limited exercise variety | Combine hip-dominant and knee-dominant exercises for comprehensive coverage  |
| Performing NHE before training | Traditional warm-up habits | Consider performing after training, though evidence on timing is mixed  |
| Neglecting sprint exposure | Focus only on gym work | Include high-speed running and sprinting as part of prevention  |

