## Sample Exercises

### Exercise 1: Nordic Hamstring Exercise (NHE) – Foundation
- **Target:** Hamstring eccentric strength (semitendinosus emphasis)
- **Execution:** Kneel with partner fixing ankles. Keep body straight from knees to shoulders. Lower body forward as slowly as possible, using hamstrings to resist. Catch with hands and push back up
- **Progression:** Follow the 13-week progression model above 

### Exercise 2: Romanian Deadlift (Hip-Dominant)
- **Target:** Biceps femoris long head, glutes, spinal erectors
- **Execution:** Stand with slight knee bend, hinge at hips, lower weight while keeping back straight, return to standing
- **Load:** Start with bodyweight, progress to light load 

### Exercise 3: Slider Leg Curls
- **Target:** Hamstring eccentric and concentric strength
- **Execution:** Lie supine with heels on sliders. Lift hips, slide heels toward glutes, then slowly extend legs out
- **Progression:** Single-leg variation

### Exercise 4: Sprint Training (On-Field)
- **Target:** Hamstring function under high-speed running conditions
- **Execution:** Progressive sprint exposures during preseason, building sprint distance and count gradually 
- **Note:** This is the most specific form of hamstring injury prevention 

