## Key Research References

- van Dyk et al.: Including NHE in prevention programmes **halves the rate of hamstring injuries** (meta-analysis of 8,459 athletes) 
- Petersen et al.: NHE reduced relative risk of HSI by **70%** in Danish professional and amateur soccer players 
- van der Horst et al.: NHE decreased relative risk of HSI by **57%** 
- Systematic review (2026): Exercise-based programmes reduce HSI risk (RR = 0.51); **high adherence (≥75%) associated with RR = 0.36** 
- FIFA 11+ study: High compliance decreased HSI risk by **78%** vs low compliance 

---

## Key Research Findings Supporting This Course

- **NHE halves hamstring injury rates** when included in prevention programmes (meta-analysis of 8,459 athletes) 
- **Exercise-based prevention programmes reduce HSI risk** by approximately 49% overall (RR = 0.51) 
- **High adherence is critical**: RR = 0.36 with ≥75% adherence, versus much weaker effects with low adherence 
- **FIFA 11+** showed the most consistent association with reduced HSI incidence vs usual training (IRR = 0.55), though certainty is low due to heterogeneity 
- **Combining hip-dominant and knee-dominant exercises** provides more comprehensive hamstring coverage 

